    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system, keeping each piece of logic in its natural home.\n\n**`MembershipLevelEvaluator`** (`service/MembershipLevelEvaluator.java`) \u2014 reworked from a \"start-at-1, +1-per-factor, cap-at-4\" scheme into a two-stage scorer:\n- `pointsFor(owner)` computes the score: **+2** email, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** household of 3+, **+3** tenure > 365 days (starting at 0).\n- `levelFor(owner)` delegates to `pointsFor` then maps via a private `levelForPoints`: 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+).\n- The new household factor reuses the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersInHousehold(...)` (injected via constructor, matching the `BulkSignupWarningEvaluator` pattern) rather than duplicating any lookup. Tenure still uses the injected `Clock`. Each weight/threshold is a named constant.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` so both fields are returned: `membershipPoints` (via `pointsFor`) alongside the existing `membershipLevel` (via `levelFor`).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` property (int32, 0-8, read-only) that generates the DTO field MapStruct populates, and updated the `membershipLevel` description to reflect that it is now derived from the points buckets.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsPointsAndLevel`) \u2014 a fresh owner with email + no namesake + single-member household + zero tenure \u2014 now correctly yields `membershipPoints = 3` and `membershipLevel = 2`.\n\nOne implementation note: `MembershipLevelEvaluator` now has two constructors (the public DI one and a package-private one taking a `Clock` for tests), so I annotated the primary constructor with `@Autowired` \u2014 otherwise Spring couldn't pick one and failed to instantiate the bean.",
