    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners` (handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:183`).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Authorization\n- `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Binding / `@Valid` pass (before the method body; failures accumulate into one `BindingResult` \u2192 400)\n\n**Bean Validation constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:**\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to two space/`'`/`-` separated parts).\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`).\n3. `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`.\n4. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n5. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`.\n6. `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(max 255)` + `@Email` (syntactic).\n7. `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`.\n8. `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (nested; no effective constraints).\n\n**Custom validators registered on the binder** (`initOwnerFieldsBinder`, `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:151`), in this registration order:\n9. `OwnerFieldsValidator` \u2014 rejects blank/whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked *after* address normalization), `city`, `telephone`.\n10. `PostcodeValidator` \u2014 when postcode is present and 4 digits, it must be valid for the city's region (`RegionPostcodes.isValidForCity`); otherwise rejected.\n11. `DisposableEmailDomainValidator` \u2014 when email present, rejects known disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Method body (`addOwner`), strictly in this order\n\n12. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`). *Side effect:* leaves `id`, `pets`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf` unset.\n13. **Normalize address** (`addressNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 `setAddress`). *Side effect:* trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`.\n14. **Validate registration date** (`registrationDateValidator.validate`) \u2014 a supplied date after today throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n15. **Default registration date** \u2014 if null, use `LocalDate.now()`.\n16. **Business-day adjust** (`businessDayAdjuster.toBusinessDay` \u2192 `setRegistrationDate`). *Side effect:* a Saturday/Sunday date rolls forward to Monday.\n17. **Normalize telephone** (`telephoneNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 `setTelephone`). *Side effect + validation:* strip spaces/dashes/brackets, resolve to E.164 (default country code `+61`, drop one leading `0`); must be 8\u201315 digits and satisfy the per-country national-length rule, else `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n18. **Normalize email** (`emailNormalizer.normalize` \u2192 `setEmail`). *Side effect:* trim + lower-case, or `null` if blank.\n19. **Daily registration limit** (`dailyRegistrationLimitValidator.validate`) \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already registered on that (adjusted) date \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitExceededException`.\n20. **City capacity** (`cityCapacityValidator.validate`) \u2014 rejects if the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException`.\n21. **Compute household id** (`households.householdId` \u2192 `setHouseholdId`). *Side effect:* deterministic SHA-256-derived id from normalized last name + postcode.\n22. **Read `sharesHousehold` flag** from the DTO.\n23. **Household duplicate check** (`householdDuplicateValidator.validate`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, rejects when another owner already shares this household id \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (409).\n24. **Possible-duplicate handling** (branch):\n    - if `sharesHousehold` \u2192 set `possibleDuplicate = false`;\n    - else `possibleDuplicateDetector.detect` \u2014 *side effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate`, and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest existing owner with the same last name + postcode but a different telephone.\n25. **Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`, `ClinicServiceImpl.java:241`). *Side effects, for a new owner:*\n    - if no `customerCode`: derive region (`Locality.forOwner`) and set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (`CustomerCodeGenerator`);\n    - if `namesakeCount` null: count same-last-name owners (case-insensitive) and set `namesakeCount` (`namesakeCounter.count`);\n    - `ownerRepository.save`.\n26. **Audit log** (`ownerAuditLogger.logCreated`) \u2014 *side effect:* writes an `AUDIT` info line with `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`.\n27. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (derives `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `ageBand`, etc.), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return `201 Created`.\n\nNote on Phase 1 ordering: Bean Validation constraints and the three binder-registered validators all run in the same validation pass and their errors are collected together; the numbering within Phase 1 reflects registration order, not a strict short-circuit sequence. The Phase 2 steps, by contrast, run in exactly the listed order and short-circuit on the first exception thrown."
